#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:103
msgid ""
"As we want to compare various models, we now create a list of all the models "
"we wish to solve:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"models = [\n"
"    pybamm.lithium_ion.SPM(),\n"
"    pybamm.lithium_ion.SPMe(),\n"
"    pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN(),\n"
"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:128
msgid ""
"We will loop over the list, creating and solving simulations as we go (in "
"the same way we learned in `Tutorial 1 <./tutorial-1-how-to-run-a-model."
"ipynb>`__), and storing the solved simulations in the list ``sims``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"sims = []\n"
"for model in models:\n"
"    sim = pybamm.Simulation(model)\n"
"    sim.solve([0, 3600])\n"
"    sims.append(sim)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:153
msgid ""
"We can now pass our list of simulations to the ``dynamic_plot`` method, "
"which has similar syntax to the ``sim.plot()`` method we used earlier and "
"will plot the different solutions in the same figure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[4]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "pybamm.dynamic_plot(sims)"
msgstr ""

